 "structural_change": "S81-CAPC4 10-20 structural clock redesign of capc2/capc4 (CLOCKING STANDARD 10-18, safe item 7): LANDED parent from tools/landed_parent/lp.py (spec tools/landed_parent/specs/ot_s81sl_capc5.json). u_rt (boundary insertion 234..298 TT) gets its own clock region ck_rt; trees / ED24 / LD16 / input face registers share region ck_core. The 12 crossings into u_rt (W word, E word, cfg) are ot_pl_land 4-slot rings (+3 edges, fixed, no backpressure); outputs leave through out_regs. Replaces the single core_clk root whose conservative child envelope was TT109.1/FF122.4 (11 compensation variants all failed dual-corner 80). VARIANT B (after gate 02:48 FAIL: two half-tile-spanning trees, soft spread TT 183/127): THREE local regions -- cw (W input regs + u_ld3 + u_tw, W-top), core (E input regs + cfg regs + u_te + u_ed + N output regs, E-top) and rt (u_rt + S output regs, bottom); rt_w/rt_e pins confined to the top half beside their trees; N outputs landed out of rt (+3: N leaves W+8, S leaves W+5); region clocks ck_cw (W face), ck_core (E face), ck_rt (S face).",
 "why_floorplan": "Same closed children and 43.2-lattice origins as CLOSED capc2 (rt 43.2,43.2; tw 43.2,302.4; te 216,302.4; ED 216,216; LD 43.2,216) and the same 329.184 x 411.48 outline and face pin ranges (clk -> ck_core, ck_rt beside it on S). Region core = top half (trees, ED, LD) + W/E/N input face registers; region rt = u_rt (bottom) + landing readers + output registers. ~1,937 landing flops + 1,172 face flops sit in the full-width south band and the 56/39 um channels; fill set by the children and lattice.",
